Azure autoscale allows supported workloads to adjust capacity according to demand. Instead of maintaining maximum capacity continuously, resources can increase or decrease based on predefined conditions.

Autoscaling can be based on factors such as:

* CPU utilization
* Request volume
* Queue length
* Schedule
* Application workload

For example, an online ticket booking platform may increase application instances when traffic rises during a major event and reduce capacity after demand returns to normal.

A real-life use case is an e-commerce website automatically scaling during a festival sale and reducing resources afterward.

Autoscaling improves application responsiveness while helping organizations avoid paying for unnecessary capacity during low-demand periods.
